Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Upstream PR pingdotgg/t3code#34005 (branch feat/queue-send-all, 8a3911e583,
600af973b8, 7e554681ce, 1cc1223dea), squashed.

Behaviours:
- With two or more queued messages the queue footer shows two actions next to
  the "Show all N queued" toggle (the toggle still appears only when the list
  is collapsible): "Send one by one" (ghost) and "Send all as one" (outline,
  arrow-up icon). Each sits in a tooltip that says what it will do or why it
  is disabled. A single queued message shows neither.
- Send all as one dispatches a new server command, queued-run.merge, with the
  queued run ids in delivery order (at least two). The server folds the queue
  into its first message: texts joined by blank lines in order, attachments
  and context records moved onto the first message, and the other queued runs
  cancelled. On success the client sends the first run through the existing
  send-now path: resume when the thread is stopped, promote-to-steer into the
  running turn otherwise. A failed merge sends nothing.
- Merging keeps an "Ultrathink:" prefix once at the top when any part has it,
  drops attachment-only bootstrap prompts from the body and restores the
  bootstrap prompt when the merged message has attachments but no text.
- The server rejects a merge, leaving the queue as it was, with the reason as
  the command's rejection cause when: a run id is not queued ("Run <id> is not
  queued."), the ids are not a contiguous slice of the delivery queue in order
  (a message queued, moved or removed since the client looked, or a queued
  notification between them: "The queue changed. Review it and try again."),
  a part is a guest's message, a message from an agent or automation
  (non-user creator, scheduled task, sender thread, idle compaction, workflow
  script, delegated completion, notification), a slash command, a
  fresh-session message, a plan or continuation message, or uses another model
  than the first; parts share an attachment; the attachments exceed the
  provider limit; two parts carry different context records with the same id;
  the combined context exceeds the record limit, or exceeds the serialized
  context limit the event store enforces ("Queued messages carry too much
  context to send as one.", instead of a generic failure at commit).
  Delegated-completion runs are not part of the queue the command sees.
- Send all as one is disabled with a reason while a queued message is edited
  or saving, while another queue action runs, when the environment does not
  advertise queuedRunMerge in its server config ("Update this environment to
  send queued messages as one."), when a notification waits between the user's
  queued messages ("A notification is waiting between these messages."), when
  the messages cannot be combined (the server's reasons above), or when the
  running turn cannot take a message ("The current turn can't take messages
  right now."). On agents that steer by restarting the turn it stays enabled,
  so the whole queue costs one restart. During a compaction it skips the
  compaction.
- Send one by one resumes the whole queue when the thread is stopped (one
  resume command), or promotes each queued message into the running turn in
  order and stops at the first failure. It is disabled with a reason when the
  turn cannot take messages, during a compaction ("Send them as one to skip
  the compaction."), on agents that restart their turn for every steer ("This
  agent restarts its turn for every message. Send them as one instead."), and
  when a queued message cannot join the running turn as it is (fresh session,
  slash command, another model than the running turn, or attachments the
  provider does not accept while steering).
- Queue actions run one at a time: a single in-flight guard and busy run id
  cover Send now, Send all as one and Send one by one.
- A new keybinding command thread.sendQueuedMessagesAsOne ("Queue: Send All
  Queued as One Message" in Keybindings settings, no default shortcut) sends
  all as one from the chat view; the tooltip shows its shortcut when bound. It
  does nothing on a draft route or when the action is disabled.
- The server advertises queuedRunMerge: true in its config, counts the command
  as the queue.merge feature in telemetry, and rejects a merge of a queued
  guest message like an edit of one.
- isSlashCommandText moves into @t3tools/shared/model and is reused by the
  Claude ultrathink prefix and by the queue checks.
- The composer and keybindings user guides describe both actions, when Send
  all as one is unavailable, and the new keybinding.

