Tests:
- apps/server/src/orchestration-v2/runtimeLayer.test.ts: a merge case queues
  three messages behind an active run (two sharing an image context record,
  two images), rejects a reordered, skipping, unknown-run and active-run merge
  with their causes, merges all three into "First\n\nSecond\n\nThird" with
  both attachments and deduplicated context, cancels the other two, rejects a
  second merge of a cancelled run, and delivers the merged message once the
  active run completes. A second case refuses a merge across a queued
  notification and leaves runs and messages unchanged. A table refuses an
  agent's, an automation's and a notification message, conflicting context,
  context over the serialized limit, a command, a fresh-session message and
  another model, each with its cause and an unchanged queue.
- apps/server/src/orchestration-v2/GuestShare.test.ts: the queued guest
  message case also rejects merging it with the owner's queued message and
  keeps the owner's run queued.
- packages/client-runtime/src/state/threadWorkflows.test.ts: a table derives
  the Send all as one and Send one by one reasons for a steerable turn, a
  restart-steering agent, model and attachment mismatches, compaction,
  notifications before, between and after the user's messages, a stopped
  thread, a turn not yet steerable, guest, agent, command, fresh-session,
  plan and other-model messages, and attachments the turn cannot take.
- apps/web/src/components/chat/QueuedRunsControl.browser.test.tsx: Send all as
  one merges then steers into a running turn or resumes a stopped thread;
  sends nothing when the merge fails; Send one by one steers in order and
  stops at the first failure, or resumes the whole stopped queue with one
  command; both actions are limited while editing, while saving and when the
  server would refuse, and Send all as one when the environment does not
  advertise or disables merging (with its tooltip); a single queued message
  shows no actions.
